# What the Go generator writes that this repository does not want.
#
# applabext/ is ours, protected from regeneration: it is the hand-written helper
# layer — the chunked upload, the followed log, the archive and the build-id
# lookup the generator cannot write.
#
# go.mod is deliberately NOT listed, so the generator's own module file is kept.
# The generated client's runtime imports third-party packages, and folding those
# into this repository's go.mod would add a SDK's dependencies to the server's
# dependency graph — the server builds none of this and should not carry it. A
# module here means `sdk/golang` is built on its own, which is also why
# hack/sdk-compile.sh runs its tests separately.
#
# Everything else is noise this repository has its own answer for: CI for services
# AppLab does not use, a push script for a repository layout that is not this one,
# per-operation Markdown that duplicates the specification, and a test file per
# model that nothing runs.

# Ours, protected from regeneration.
applabext/

# The generator's own tests, which this repository does not run.
*_test.go
test/

# CI and publishing for a standalone project; this SDK lives inside AppLab.
.gitlab-ci.yml
.travis.yml
git_push.sh
.github/

# Documentation the generator emits alongside the code.
docs/

# The repository's own ignore rules are managed at the root.
.gitignore
